.TH SVXCONNECT-QT 1 "August 2026" "svxconnect-qt" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
svxconnect\-qt \- desktop client for SvxLink reflectors
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B svxconnect\-qt
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ URL ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B svxconnect\-qt
connects to a SvxLink reflector over mutual TLS and carries AES\-128\-GCM
encrypted Opus audio over UDP. It monitors several talkgroups at once, shows who
is talking on which, switches between them by priority or by hand, and
transmits.
.PP
It shares one identity with
.BR svxconnect (1):
the same configuration file, the same client certificate and a shared run lock.
Only one of the two may hold the reflector connection at a time; the other
refuses to start and names the process in the way.
.PP
Enrol once with
.B "svxconnect \-\-enroll"
before first use.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-c \fIfile\fR, \fB\-\-config \fIfile\fR
Use this configuration file instead of the default.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH PUSH-TO-TALK
Hold the on\-screen button to transmit, or press
.B Space
to toggle;
.B Escape
always stops.
.PP
A global shortcut is registered with the desktop through the XDG global\-
shortcuts portal, so it works while the window is unfocused, on both Wayland and
X11, with no elevated permission. It defaults to
.BR Meta+Return .
Change it in the desktop's own keyboard settings, where SVXConnect appears as a
shortcut component; the application follows whatever is set there.
.PP
To use CapsLock as the modifier, first make it a real one \(em on KDE Plasma,
System Settings, Keyboard, Key Bindings, Caps Lock behavior, "Make Caps Lock an
additional Hyper". CapsLock+Enter is then exactly the default shortcut.
.PP
The shortcut belongs to the running process, so closing the window hides
.B svxconnect\-qt
to the system tray rather than quitting. Quit from the tray icon.
.PP
Transmission stops automatically after
.I tx_timeout_sec
seconds, 120 by default, so a stuck key cannot leave the transmitter on.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/svxconnect/svxconnect.conf
Configuration, shared with
.BR svxconnect (1).
Editable from Preferences, or by hand \(em comments and layout are preserved.
.TP
.I ~/.config/svxconnect/pki/
Client key and certificate.
.TP
.I ~/.config/SVXConnect/SVXConnect.conf
Settings belonging only to the desktop client: window geometry and the
push\-to\-talk mode.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/svxconnect/ctl
Control FIFO. Write
.B "ptt on"
or
.B "ptt off"
to it from a script, a foot switch or a compositor key binding.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SVX_WINDOW_ONLY
If set, open the window without starting the reflector core. For working on the
interface on a machine with no certificate.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR svxconnect (1)
.PP
Full documentation at
.UR https://svxconnect.app
.UE .
.SH AUTHOR
Written by Joeri Van Dooren, ON6URE.
